<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
	Privacy manifest. Required at submission since spring 2024.

	Volumen collects nothing. There is no account, no server, no analytics and
	no network code of any kind: books move from the user's own Files app to
	the phone and from the phone to the watch over WatchConnectivity, which is
	a local link between two devices the same person owns. Bookmarks live in a
	JSON file inside the app's own container.

	NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes is therefore an empty array rather than absent.
	Absent and empty mean the same thing to App Store Connect, but an empty
	array is a statement and a missing key is an oversight, and a reviewer
	cannot tell the difference between the second one and forgetting.

	NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp is declared because
	FileManager.attributesOfItem(atPath:) reads each audio file's size when
	deriving its stable id (LibraryStore.identity and Player.fileMatches).
	3B52.1 is the correct reason: those files are inside the app's own
	container, and the value never leaves the device.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>3B52.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
